{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2627 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "65d81983ad5b721598e68bd86d038c398d6954e470a7e1b88de00b8b3981ca16" :edb/db-before-t 2626 :edb/db-after-t 2627 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535939 50 #inst "2026-10-09T11:01:19.009Z" 13194139535939 true] [17592186119685 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375398 13194139535939 true] [17592186119685 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375405 13194139535939 true] [17592186119685 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375412 13194139535939 true] [17592186119686 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375419 13194139535939 true] [17592186119686 1020 #edb/ref 17592186375426 13194139535939 true] [17592186375398 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375399 13194139535939 true] [17592186375398 1089 "q-162397" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375398 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535939 true] [17592186375398 1100 "Find the radius of the curvature for the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{3},\\,1-t⟩$ at $t=1.$" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375398 1113 #uuid "ed79e8c4-1810-5f03-9522-5e9ee679d4fa" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375398 1145 "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nThe radius of curvature $R$ is defined as\n$R(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}.$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{3},\\,y(t)=1-t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =3{t}^{2},\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =6t,\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|3{t}^{2}\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 6t|}{{((3t)^{2}+(1)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6|t|}{{(9{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(1) & =\\frac{6|1|}{{(9(1)^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{{(10)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(1) & =\\frac{1}{κ(1)}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{10}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375400 13194139535939 true] [17592186375399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375401 13194139535939 true] [17592186375399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375402 13194139535939 true] [17592186375399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375403 13194139535939 true] [17592186375399 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375404 13194139535939 true] [17592186375399 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535939 true] [17592186375399 1041 "selection" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375399 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375401 13194139535939 true] [17592186375399 1110 #uuid "5c314077-8489-5814-b6ff-baba0d5a0057" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375400 1034 "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{5}" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535939 true] [17592186375400 1111 #uuid "113fa98b-7e90-5296-b84b-7ad73c92c7f0" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375401 1034 "\\frac{5\\sqrt{10}}{3}" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375401 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535939 true] [17592186375401 1111 #uuid "4c84bfa9-2b9f-5e84-a7f3-342b0bb1c5a3" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375402 1034 "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{5}" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375402 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535939 true] [17592186375402 1111 #uuid "d7893014-dd5c-5f6e-b93d-500e216b395e" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375403 1034 "\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}}{2}" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375403 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535939 true] [17592186375403 1111 #uuid "e03b4be3-5c12-534c-a489-a813734e31e5" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375404 1034 "5\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375404 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535939 true] [17592186375404 1111 #uuid "f47e8030-9b2f-556b-bc14-9ddcf243d206" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375405 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375406 13194139535939 true] [17592186375405 1089 "q-162404" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375405 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535939 true] [17592186375405 1100 "Find the radius of curvature for the curve $r(t)=({t}^{2}-1)\\,i+(1-t)\\,j$ at $t=\\frac{1}{2}.$" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375405 1113 #uuid "29db884d-f24f-5424-973a-7e7c3098abfe" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375405 1145 "The curvature $κ(t)$ of a plane curve $r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{|{x}^{′}(t){y}^{″}(t)-{y}^{′}(t){x}^{″}(t)|}{([{x}^{′}(t)]^{2}+[{y}^{′}(t)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nThe radius of curvature $R$ is defined as\n$R(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}.$\n\nAlong our curve, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-1,\\,y(t)=1-t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the derivatives of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =2t,\\, & {y}^{′}(t) & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =2,\\, & {y}^{″}(t) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|2t\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 2|}{{((2t)^{2}+(-1)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{(4{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{2}{{(4{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{(1+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=\\frac{1}{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{κ(\\frac{1}{2})}=\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375407 13194139535939 true] [17592186375406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375408 13194139535939 true] [17592186375406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375409 13194139535939 true] [17592186375406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375410 13194139535939 true] [17592186375406 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375411 13194139535939 true] [17592186375406 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535939 true] [17592186375406 1041 "selection" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375406 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375407 13194139535939 true] [17592186375406 1110 #uuid "93907cfe-e575-578b-afea-70371bb607a3" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375407 1034 "\\sqrt{2