vature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{|2(1+t)\\cdot 2-(-2(1-t))\\cdot 2|}{{(\\,(2(1+t))^{2}+(2(1-t))^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{(8+8{t}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(0) & =\\frac{8}{{(8+8(0)^{2})}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{(8+0)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{1}{κ(0)}=2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375414 13194139535939 true] [17592186375413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375415 13194139535939 true] [17592186375413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375416 13194139535939 true] [17592186375413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375417 13194139535939 true] [17592186375413 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375418 13194139535939 true] [17592186375413 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535939 true] [17592186375413 1041 "selection" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375413 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375418 13194139535939 true] [17592186375413 1110 #uuid "2696a603-3060-5aba-87e7-751979e9a935" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375414 1034 "\\sqrt[3]{4}" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375414 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535939 true] [17592186375414 1111 #uuid "f084a609-33b1-550f-8035-8938e3a8869f" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375415 1034 "2\\sqrt[3]{2}" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375415 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535939 true] [17592186375415 1111 #uuid "833ae50e-3658-5883-b5aa-3d37893739de" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375416 1034 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375416 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535939 true] [17592186375416 1111 #uuid "d8eddfa4-0f66-5842-84a3-70b6639e2bd9" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375417 1034 "4\\sqrt[3]{2}" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535939 true] [17592186375417 1111 #uuid "ed71f44e-3adb-5719-a944-b27d60c25a6f" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375418 1034 "2\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535939 true] [17592186375418 1111 #uuid "0c8e0038-3ef5-5231-8611-ed7c6a67146d" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375419 1017 #edb/ref 17592186375420 13194139535939 true] [17592186375419 1089 "q-162532" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375419 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535939 true] [17592186375419 1100 "Find the signed curvature of the curve $y=x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ at $x=\\pi .$" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375419 1113 #uuid "158b5a12-e0e4-56c7-80c7-4700e06df09f" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375419 1145 "The signed curvature $k(x)$ of a plane curve $y=y(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nk(x)=\\frac{{y}^{″}(x)}{(1+[{y}^{′}(x)]^{2})^{3/2}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${y}^{′}(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x):$\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,{y}^{″}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting these into the formula for the signed curvature, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k(x) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{[1+{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}^{2}]}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature at $x=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k(0) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{{[1+{(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))}^{2}]}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{{2}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375421 13194139535939 true] [17592186375420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375422 13194139535939 true] [17592186375420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375423 13194139535939 true] [17592186375420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375424 13194139535939 true] [17592186375420 1000 #edb/ref 17592186375425 13194139535939 true] [17592186375420 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535939 true] [17592186375420 1041 "selection" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375420 1104 #edb/ref 17592186375421 13194139535939 true] [17592186375420 1110 #uuid "3f3961c7-a34f-5cd8-b14a-5d66c9a394e5" 13194139535939 true] [17592186375421 1034 "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}" 1319